glean maxwell was found guilty of  charges tied to jeffrey epstein's sex  trafficking ring a new york jury  convicted the british socialite of  grooming minors for sexual abuse at the  hands of epstein it was hard to see if  she was showing any real emotion because  there was a mask over her face but i can  tell you within moments of hearing  guilty on count one not guilty on count  two and guilty on those other four  counts she sort of took a deep breath  and  looked as though she was pouring herself  some water the charges stemmed from  interactions ranging from 1994 to 2004.  maxwell was romantically involved and  later worked for epstein during that  time the prosecution argued that maxwell  was epstein's partner in crime and  critical to his alleged sex trafficking  operation throughout the two-week trial  jurors heard from four alleged victims  who claimed maxwell recruited them for  epstein and that she normalized and  sometimes even participated in the abuse  epstein committed suicide in august 2019  while awaiting trial  following the verdict u.s attorney  damien williams read in a statement in  part quote i want to commend the bravery  of the girls now grown women who stepped  out of the shadows and into the  courtroom their courage and willingness  to face their abuser made this case in  today's result possible again this is a  big day for a number of women not just  the four that with the center of this  trial but the dozens of women who  accused jeffrey epstein of sexual abuse  and never got to see his case go to  trial  maxwell was found guilty of five of the  six federal counts and she now faces a  maximum sentence of 65 years in prison  it's absolutely a repudiation of the  defense's tactic here the defense  frankly i think trying to blame the  victims saying their memories were  faulty saying that they were really  motivated by money her attorney has  announced plans to appeal the verdict so  in this case the guilt phase obviously  is over at least on the trial court  level and the next phase will be  sentencing so the prosecution will come  forward with a sentencing memo the  defense will say well look we think  there's some mitigating factors here but  let's be honest glenn maxwell faces  years if not decades in federal prison
 

